{
  "case_id": "2009-08-969",
  "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Possessory and use taxes are extremely difficult to collect, even under the best of circumstances. Indeed, here the city alleges in its second amended complaint that it only collected 40 cents on the dollar, and its response claims a collection rate of 55 cents on the dollar. Yet it wants to collect 300 cents on the dollar from my clients, who never owed these taxes in the first place."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "City of New York",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yet reinstating the one RICO claim was improper because the city does not have standing to sue, based on the injuries that it has alleged. It does not have standing because the city's claim that it lost the sovereign opportunity to tax is not an injury to -- to business, and it's not an injury to property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Why -- why isn't the money property?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: There is no such adjective -- I know we have used it, but there is no such adjective as \"choate.\" There is \"inchoate,\" but the opposite of \"inchoate\" is not \"choate.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BARNHOUSE: The -- the -- what they've alleged here is not that they've lost the taxes, but that they've lost the opportunity to tax. Moreover, they should not be able to reach that point because the allegations themselves are that the injury is not proximate. It is the city itself --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How many people who buy cigarettes out of State come back to their home State and voluntarily pay the use tax?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Isn't there some exemption, anyway, for a couple of cartons?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Barnhouse",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the city here, as I -- as stated in the record, says even under the best of circumstances, Justice Ginsburg, it collects only 40 cents on the dollar, perhaps as much as 55 --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Do we know -- you gave an instance in your brief or two instances of successful attempts to recoup from the taxpayer, that is the cigarette buyer. Did those come about because the city received the Jenkins Act list from the State? How did the city get --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Koerner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KOERNER: Here's what would be worth it: If we can stop the fraudulent practices that these sellers represent through the treble damages. The only benefit that these Internet sellers have is the cost saving as a consequence of the tax saving."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Koerner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
      "evidence_id": "ev-53bdbc82bc5d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KOERNER: But in the proximate cause equation, as you yourself have defined it, meaning the Court, you've talked about unlawful issues and lawful issues. And as I indicated, where there's a combination you don't want a Court to weigh what's lawful and unlawful. But here our injury -- injury is solely the result of an unlawful use. There are no intervening factors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-969",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "53bdbc82bc5db568acaed4b1a6f963eceee33532a9e81b3424a9f94131311457",
